    "detailed_description": "Isle of the Dead is a timeless journey, starting from an everyday apartment towards our final destination, guided by Charon, ferryman of the Underworld. <br />\r\nThis VR experience is a loose recreation of the eponymous work painted in 1883 by the Swiss symbolist painter Arnold B\u00f6cklin. The famous masterpiece also inspired a symphonic poem by Rachmaninov, which makes a perfect soundtrack to accompany the experience. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nIsle of the Dead is part of the collection \u00ab ARTE TRIPS \u00bb, a series of immersive VR experiences that take you into masterpieces from 16th to 20th century by well-known painters. <br />\r\n<br />\r\n\u2022\tBest Story in VR at Venice Film Festival 2018<br />\r\n\u2022\tAudience Award at Entrevues Belfort 2018 <br />\r\n\u2022\tSpecial Jury VR award at FilmGate Miami 2018 <br />\r\n\u2022\tBest Virtual Reality Short Film at China International New Media Short Film Festival <br />\r\n<br />\r\nA VR experience directed by Benjamin Nuel<br />\r\nWritten by Benjamin Nuel et Cl\u00e9mence Madeleine-Perdrillat<br />\r\nA coproduction Les Produits Frais, ARTE France.<br />\r\nWith the participation of CNC \u2013 New Media Fund<br />\r\n<br />\r\nLength: 8 minutes",
